# VIDEO POLICY — no CDN (cost); GitHub Pages hosts the clips directly.
# Every referenced clip is committed (all are under GitHub's 100 MB/file limit). We ONLY ignore
# clips we never ship, so a stray heavy file can't sneak into history.
#
# Ignored, with reason:
assets/forge.mp4          # the old 140 MB monolith — REPLACED by forge_cut_1..N (over the file limit anyway)
assets/hero3_intro.mp4    # not referenced by the page
#
# ⚠️ History note: re-rendering a clip (same filename, overwritten) keeps the OLD copy in git
# history forever → the repo grows with each re-render. If it bloats, do a deliberate
# history-rewrite (git filter-repo) in its own session with a backup first. Prefer committing a
# clip only once it's final.

# dev-only tooling (lives in StormForge_web, never shipped to the Pages repo)
serve.py
make_web.sh
check.sh
__pycache__/
*.pyc
webdev/
archieve/

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
